worker_module_budget
  module "formal_ai_worker_20.js"
  ceiling 1461
  rationale "Part of the mechanically split browser mirror of the Rust solver. The synchronous handler capability bindings moved to formal_ai_worker_dispatch.js; this shard keeps orchestration, the issue #710 browser parity recoveries, and since issue #1138 B8 / plan 09 leaves 13-15 the worker handler registry: the exact-permutation mirror of data/seed/handler-precedence.lino that binds the seed vocabulary (verifiable_task included) to worker implementations, which is why the ceiling moved from 1308 to 1459. Plan 09 leaf 41 then grew it to 1465: the registry permutation now reads the `handler <name>` row ids that carry the rank links instead of raw child names, mirroring MethodRegistry::from_store. The comment and call were re-compressed (1461) and the ceiling re-baselined to that measured value; the growth is the leaf-41 id-and-rank read, not silent regrowth."
